    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 110,
     "s": "[Enter Aegisthus."
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 110,
     "s": "Aegisthus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 110,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Hither and not unsummoned have I come;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For a new rumour, borne by stranger men",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Arriving hither, hath attained mine ears,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of hap unwished-for, even Orestes’ death.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "This were new sorrow, a blood-bolter’d load",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Laid on the house that doth already bow",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Beneath a former wound that festers deep.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Dare I opine these words have truth and life?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Or are they tales, of woman’s terror born,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That fly in the void air, and die disproved?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Canst thou tell aught, and prove it to my soul?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 111,
     "s": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 111,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "What we have heard, we heard; go thou within",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Thyself to ask the strangers of their tale.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Strengthless are tidings, thro’ another heard;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Question is his to whom the tale is brought.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 111,
     "s": "Aegisthus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 111,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "I too will meet and test the messenger,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Whether himself stood witness of the death,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Or tells it merely from dim rumour learnt:",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "None shall cheat me, whose soul hath watchful eyes.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 111,
     "s": "[Exit."
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 111,
     "s": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 111,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Zeus, Zeus! what word to me is given?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "What cry or prayer, invoking heaven,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Shall first by me be utterèd?",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "What speech of craft—nor all revealing,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Nor all too warily concealing—",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Ending my speech, shall aid the deed?",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "For lo! in readiness is laid",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The dark emprise, the rending blade;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Blood-dropping daggers shall achieve",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "The dateless doom of Atreus’ name,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Or—kindling torch and joyful flame",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "In sign of new-won liberty—",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Once more Orestes shall retrieve",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "His father’s wealth, and, throned on high,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Shall hold the city’s fealty.",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "So mighty is the grasp whereby,",
       "i": 1
      },
      {
       "s": "Heaven-holpen, he shall trip and throw",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Unseconded, a double foe.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Ho for the victory!",
       "i": 2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 111,
     "s": "[A loud cry within."
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "Voice of Aegisthus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 112,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Help, help, alas!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 112,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Ho there, ho! how is’t within?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Is’t done? is’t over? Stand we here aloof",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "While it is wrought, that guiltless we may seem",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of this dark deed; with death is strife fulfilled.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "[Enter a slave."
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "Slave"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 112,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "O woe, O woe, my lord is done to death!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Woe, woe, and woe again, Aegisthus gone!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Hasten, fling wide the doors, unloose the bolts",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of the queen’s chamber. O for some young strength",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To match the need! but aid availeth nought",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To him laid low for ever. Help, help, help!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Sure to deaf ears I shout, and call in vain",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To slumber ineffectual. What ho!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The queen! how fareth Clytemnestra’s self?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Her neck too, hers, is close upon the steel,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And soon shall sink, hewn thro’ as justice wills.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "[Enter Clytemnestra."
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 112,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "What ails thee, raising this ado for us?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "Slave"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 112,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "I say the dead are come to slay the living.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 112,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Alack, I read thy riddles all too clear—",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "We slew by craft and by like craft shall die.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Swift, bring the axe that slew my lord of old;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I’ll know anon or death or victory—",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "So stands the curse, so I confront it here.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 112,
     "s": "[Enter Orestes, his sword dropping with blood."
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Thee too I seek: for him what’s done will serve.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Woe, woe! Aegisthus, spouse and champion, slain!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "What, lov’st the man? then in his grave lie down,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Be his in death, desert him nevermore!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Stay, child, and fear to strike. O son, this breast",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Pillowed thine head full oft, while, drowsed with sleep,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Thy toothless mouth drew mother’s milk from me.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Can I my mother spare? speak, Pylades.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Pylades"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Where then would fall the hest Apollo gave",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "At Delphi, where the solemn compact sworn?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Choose thou the hate of all men, not of gods.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Thou dost prevail; I hold thy counsel good.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "[To Clytemnestra."
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Follow; I will to slay thee at his side.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With him whom in his life thou lovedst more",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Than Agamemnon, sleep in death, the meed",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For hate where love, and love where hate was due!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "I nursed thee young; must I forego mine eld?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 113,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 113,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Thou slew’st my father; shalt thou dwell with me?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Fate bore a share in these things, O my child!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Fate also doth provide this doom for thee.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Beware, O child, a parent’s dying curse.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "A parent who did cast me out to ill!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Not cast thee out, but to a friendly home.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Born free, I was by twofold bargain sold.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Where then the price that I received for thee?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The price of shame; I taunt thee not more plainly.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Nay, but recount thy father’s lewdness too.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Home-keeping, chide not him who toils without.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "’Tis hard for wives to live as widows, child.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 114,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 114,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "The absent husband toils for them at home.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Thou growest fain to slay thy mother, child.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Nay, ’tis thyself wilt slay thyself, not I.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Beware thy mother’s vengeful hounds from hell.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "How shall I ’scape my father’s, sparing thee?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Living, I cry as to a tomb, unheard.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "My father’s fate ordains this doom for thee.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Clytemnestra"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Ah, me! this snake it was I bore and nursed.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Orestes"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Ay, right prophetic was thy visioned fear.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Shameful thy deed was—die the death of shame!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "[Exit, driving Clytemnestra before him"
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 115,
     "s": "Chorus"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Lo, even for these I mourn, a double death:",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Yet since Orestes, driven on by doom,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Thus crowns the height of murders manifold,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I say, ’tis well that not in night and death",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Should sink the eye and light of this our home.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 115,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "There came on Priam’s race and name",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "A vengeance; though it tarried long,",
       "i": 3
      },
      {
       "s": "With heavy doom it came.",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "Came, too, on Agamemnon’s hall",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "A lion-pair, twin swordsmen strong.",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "And last, the heritage doth fall",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "To him to whom from Pythian cave",
       "i": 3
      },
      {
       "s": "The god his deepest counsel gave.",
       "i": 3
      },
      {
       "s": "Cry out, rejoice! our kingly hall",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Hath ’scaped from ruin—ne’er again",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "Its ancient wealth be wasted all",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "By two usurpers, sin-defiled—",
       "i": 5
      },
      {
       "s": "An evil path of woe and bane!",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "On him who dealt the dastard blow",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Comes Craft, Revenge’s scheming child.",
       "i": 4
      },
      {
       "s": "And hand in hand with him doth go,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Eager for fight,",
       "i": 7
      },
      {
       "s": "The child of Zeus, whom men below",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Call Justice, naming her aright.",
       "i": 3
      },
      {
       "s": "And on her foes her breath",
       "i": 6
      },
      {
       "s": "Is as the blast of death;",
       "i": 6
      },
      {
       "s": "For her the god who dwells in deep recess",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Beneath Parnassus’ brow,",
       "i": 6
      },
      {
       "s": "Summons with loud acclaim",
       "i": 5
      },
      {
       "s": "To rise, though late and lame,",
       "i": 5
      },
      {
       "s": "And come with craft that worketh righteousness.",
       "i": 2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 116,
     "lines": [
      {
