    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 118,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Hark ye and learn—for what the end shall be",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "For me I know not: breaking from the curb,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "My spirit whirls me off, a conquered prey,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Borne as a charioteer by steeds distraught",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Far from the course, and madness in my breast",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Burneth to chant its song, and leap, and rave—",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Hark ye and learn, friends, ere my reason goes!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I say that rightfully I slew my mother,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "A thing God-scorned, that foully slew my sire.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And chiefest wizard of the spell that bound me",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Unto this deed I name the Pythian seer",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Apollo, who foretold that if I slew,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The guilt of murder done should pass from me;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "But if I spared, the fate that should be mine",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I dare not blazon forth—the bow of speech",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Can reach not to the mark, that doom to tell.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And now behold me, how with branch and crown",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I pass, a suppliant made meet to go",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Unto Earth’s midmost shrine, the holy ground",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of Loxias, and that renowned light",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of ever-burning fire, to ’scape the doom",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of kindred murder: to no other shrine",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "(So Loxias bade) may I for refuge turn.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Bear witness, Argives, in the aftertime,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "How came on me this dread fatality.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Living, I pass a banished wanderer hence,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To leave in death the memory of this cry.",
       "i": 0
      }
